put.description:
`system.admin` only. Sets (or, with `null`, clears) the key's own
per-minute budget. Idempotent: the same body twice leaves the same value;
the change and its audit event commit together.

post.description:
Accept (keep the customer's value): nothing is written but the decision;
the baseline already holds ours, so the next release does not raise it
again unless we change the field again.

A23-T8: a `multipart/form-data` body with a `file` part and an optional
`options` part (JSON). Stores the file and stages it in the background;
the same file for the same entity answers the job already made for it.

ApprovalStep.description:
One step of an [`ApprovalPlan`]. Parallel = a step with `mode: all`;
sequential = multiple steps — `decide_step` only advances to `steps[n+1]`
once `steps[n]` itself is satisfied.

state.description:
`requested` — recorded now, and the turn stops at its next boundary;
`already_requested` — an earlier Stop stands; `already_ended` — the
turn had already finished, and nothing was written.

ContentTemplate.description:
A reusable block-content starting point for new pages — selecting one at
page-create time copies `blocks` into the new page's `blocks_draft` once;
there is no ongoing link back to the template afterward (D-369).
